Good question.  FWIW, I have ascended all roles/races on NAO, and have
a couple of 3-in-a-rows. Distilling all the techniques I use into good
habits is a rare and worthy exercise.  I'm trying to focus more on
principles than techniques, since there are so many.  These may not be
the magic bullets you need for your first ascension (mine was a Sokoban
WoW), but I think they will get you closer.  And they're not just for
newbies.  You can see these in action watching games on NAO.  The
legendary Marvin says all games are ascendable, and doing the sometimes
tedious things can make the difference between dying and almost dying.
So here's what I see and do:

BUILD YOUR CHARACTER.  Stats, AC, resistances, intrinsics, luck.  The
more the better.  Every point counts in the early game.  Know how to
exercise or increase them and take the opportunities to do it.  Its a
matter of playing style and experience as to how buff you get, but for
ascension 1, max em out.

KNOW YOUR WEAPONS.  Be aware of your role's best options for melee and
range.  Exercise and advance the skills that will later support
artifact weapons you will get.  If its spells, work those.  In the
meantime, use the best possible weapons you can find.  That uncursed
dagger that won't stack is probably enchanted.  Throw rocks and potions
if thats all you can get.  I had to take out a black dragon in Ludios
once by hitting it with a potion of polymorph from long range.

IDENTIFY EVERYTHING.  B/U/C with pets and altars.  Price ID with shops.
 Name and call objects to help the process of elimination.  More
resources mean more choices.  Its painful to die with what you needed
to live unIDed in your pack, as everyone here can tell you.

THINK DEFENSIVELY.  This includes keeping track of HP and healing
options, using the dungeon layout/features to your advantage, not
getting surrounded, playing the angles between you and monsters, hiding
behind pets and peacefuls, going down/up soon as you see a downstair,
searching for traps, having an escape option, knowing when you can
pray, using Elbereth, and of course the time honored tradition of
running away.  Live to fight again.

WATCH YOUR WEIGHT.  Being burdened slows you down, and being stressed
or worse can easily get you killed.  Learn to make stashes, bless that
BoH, or just pitch extra junk.

FEED YOUR GOD.  HP, protection, artifacts, spellbooks, luck, its all
good.  Only bad results I have come from hitting #p instead of #o, and
not watching weight when carrying corpses to the altar.  Some folks
don't like getting crowned, but I was glad for it in my early days.

STEP AWAY FROM THE KEYBOARD.  Keeps your mind fresh.  If you're in a
dire situation, you can think about it in peace, or ask for help.
Recently, knnn, an experienced and accomplished NetHacker, did just
that after accidently creating a roomful of the toughest monster in the
game.  Or chat in #nethack, or read spoilers.

BE PERSISTENT.  Its not so much a truism that quitters never win, but
quitters never learn.  Disasters like blown up bags of holding,
mindflayer attacks, punishment, nymphs, poisoning down to STR6, pissed
off gods, etc. CAN be played through.  Really builds your ability to
play the game, even if you don't survive.


Have fun and good luck! 

